# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
# Adversarial case, M8a step 1 (panel 031).
# The quoted form is what Go, C and this project's own design.md draft wrote,
# so it is the likeliest first attempt at a module — and the whole argument for
# the bare identifier is that this attempt gets a repair rather than a lecture.
# The fix is `Certain` because it deletes two characters and leaves a program
# that parses; `use "shapes/geom"` gets the same message and NO fix, which is
# the case `use-has-a-path.hero` pins.
#
# It carried a `.fixed` until M8a step 3, and then discovery arrived: applying
# the fix leaves `use geom` naming a module with no `geom.hero` beside it, so
# the repaired program exits 1 on a DIFFERENT and true diagnostic. `.fixed`
# asserts that a certain fix leaves a program that checks clean, and in a flat
# directory of single-file cases this one cannot. It gets its `.fixed` back in
# the multi-module golden directory, where `geom.hero` can sit beside it.
use "geom"  #~ use_wants_a_name

function main()
    print(0)
